1
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,790
I'm Nao Nanao! From class 1-3!

2
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:09,960
I'm 144 centimeters tall, 
and I weigh 36 kilograms!

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:13,630
I'm a Pisces with a B blood type.
And I love green tea pudding!

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,380
Although I may not be the best manager,
I will do my utmost to support the team!

5
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,250
I hope we can get along!

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,330
Nanao is... going to be our manager?

7
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:27,670
So, how are they? Now that you've
seen them in action, what are your thoughts?

8
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:30,830
W-well... everyone on the team is amazing.

9
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:32,040
Although...

10
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:37,460
I don't think this team stands
any chance of winning actual games.

11
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:41,790
If that's what she thinks, 
then there's no mistake.

12
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,080
Huh?

13
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,580
I can guarantee that personally.

14
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,960
If you'd like, we can even 
prove it with a game.

15
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,380
You can play against our girls' team.

16
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:54,250
What?!

17
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:55,130
Why?!

18
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:57,080
Well, we could be convinced.

19
00:00:57,080 --> 00:01:02,540
If the girls agree to strip naked when we win,
then I think we could find the motivation!

20
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:06,460
Gotta put a carrot on the stick, so to speak!

21
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:07,750
Very well, then.

22
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:09,210
That's fine.

23
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,920
Then we're all agreed.

24
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:14,330
Madoka will be the one to do it.

25
00:01:14,330 --> 00:01:15,290
What?

26
00:01:22,670 --> 00:01:25,040
Then we'll play! Without holding back!

27
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:41,460
Um, okay then.

28
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:45,750
Starting now, the game between the boys' and girls'
basketball teams will officially begin!

29
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:48,040
ALL RIGHT!

30
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:05,000
Where to go? The land, sea or sky?

31
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:07,580
Ahiru no Sora

32
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:08,040
I wanna invite you to come along

33
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:12,880
The pages of our story have started to turn

34
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:18,580
If you lose your nerve then recycle it

35
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,580
And let it push you past hesitation

36
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:26,830
Give and go! With the flow

37
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:34,960
Instincts that are buried deep 
will always rear their head again

38
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:42,170
People can't just hide the 
dreams they once dreamed of

39
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:45,580
Even if these wings can't fly

40
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:52,420
We want to spread them 
wide and embrace the sky

41
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:55,750
Becoming the people who we want to be

42
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:02,420
You never know, the impossible 
could be possible tomorrow

43
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:05,880
So let's keep up the struggle

44
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,960
Happy go ducky!

45
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:23,580
The match will be two 10-minute halves.

46
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:26,040
Each team will be allowed 
to call one timeout.

47
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:29,330
The Boys' Stubbornness and Girls' Pride

48
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:28,460
The ball will be a men's size 7.

49
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:31,380
I will be the coach for the girls' team.

50
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:34,210
And Mr. Satsuki, I'd like you
to be the coach for the boy's team.

51
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:35,380
Please and thank you.

52
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:37,000
Okay. I can do that.

53
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,380
Although, I really don't know 
anything about basketball.

54
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:43,500
Are there different positions,
like there are for baseball and soccer?

55
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,750
Yes, it's similar.

56
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,790
Kurumatani:
3-pointers, drives
Natsume:
Penetrates, won't pass

57
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:50,750
The backcourt player who directs the offense
is the "Point Guard."

58
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:54,710
The players in the wings who try to score
are the "Small Forward" and the "Shooting Guard."

59
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,710
Then further inside are the 
"Center" and "Power Forward."

60
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:01,290
They plant themselves near the basket
to help secure points and rebounds.

61
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:07,330
I think the boys have already settled
into the positions that suit them the best.

62
00:04:10,670 --> 00:04:11,750
I see.

63
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:15,710
I'm curious to know, do the girls stand any chance
of winning this game?

64
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:20,130
If you look at them individually,
the boys are certainly more skilled than the girls.

65
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,080
However...

66
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:23,380
VICTORY WILL BE...

67
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,830
...OURS!

68
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:28,580
Seriously?! Only teams playing in the final round
of nationals ever get THAT intense!

69
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:51,130
Okay then, here we go!

70
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:00,380
ALL RIGHT!

71
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:05,080
Wow, Momoharu! That marks
a totally new jump record for you!

72
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,330
Oh, come on, Wakamori! Please 
take this more seriously!

73
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:12,960
Who the heck drops into
the fetal position on a jump ball?!

74
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,670
I was too scared to do anything else!

75
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:24,250
Madoka! Cover Sora so he can't
shoot any three-pointers!

76
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:25,670
Okay!

77
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:27,040
Deny defense, girls!

78
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:33,210
You better get ready.

79
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:34,830
Because here I come.

80
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:38,380
H-he's so huge!

81
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,630
I've never had to guard 
someone like this before!

82
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:43,290
Hey, Bro! Over here!

83
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:48,000
Not happening!

84
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,880
Oh, that's some solid defending.

85
00:05:50,290 --> 00:05:53,380
I guess I shouldn't be surprised,
since your team practices on a daily basis.

86
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:56,330
He's not the only one confident
about having fast footwork.

87
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:57,920
I won't be shaken off easily!

88
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:02,540
There he goes! He's changing his pace!

89
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,630
Huh?

90
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:09,420
Help!

91
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:20,420
Hell yeah! That's one point for us!

92
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:22,210
Or wait, do those count for two?

93
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:23,500
It was a two-pointer.

94
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:26,920
Excellent. I'm already starting to picture
that t-shirt of hers coming right off!

95
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,250
I'm sorry... he got by 
me like it was nothing.

96
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,380
I couldn't read his movements at all.

97
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,380
Don't worry.

98
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:35,380
We've only just gotten started.

99
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:37,630
Ugh, he's just too fast...

100
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:40,330
I couldn't even see what 
kind of move he pulled.

101
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,130
Nice one.

102
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:55,040
Go back, girls!

103
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,790
Whoa! It looks like we're 
totally overwhelming them!

104
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:03,040
Sorry about this, Sora.

105
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,670
But your weakness was outed to everyone
during that match against Maru High.

106
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:13,580
I'll just lay on pressure
until I've got him cornered on the left side!

107
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:15,710
Huh?!

108
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,210
He went left...?!

109
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,880
Perfect chance!

110
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,170
Pass me the ball, Bro!

111
00:07:27,210 --> 00:07:28,040
No way!

112
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:38,210
He's shooting from the left side?!

113
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:48,380
Aw, yeah! That's our lil' Sora!

114
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:51,210
I'd say that shot guarantees a bra
will be dropping to the floor soon!

115
00:07:51,210 --> 00:07:52,920
No comments from the peanut gallery!

116
00:07:54,420 --> 00:07:55,670
I'm so glad I sunk that one!

117
00:07:57,580 --> 00:08:01,670
Have you been practicing taking shots from the left
ever since that game with Maru High?

118
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:02,580
Yep!

119
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:06,290
And I didn't just shoot them freely.

120
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:08,920
I had Yasuhara and the others 
play defense against me.

121
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:13,040
And we didn't get to go home
until well after 10:00 because of it.

122
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:16,460
I even missed my favorite show,
"The World's Most Amazing Animals"!

123
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,670
Well, we got a good deal.

124
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:20,500
Since the squirt is going
to treat us to lunch for the next 3 months.

125
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:23,500
Uh... I don't remember agreeing 
to anything like that.

126
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,420
Wait a minute...
Are you for real? The best move there was passing me the ball.

127
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,500
Are you for real? The best move 
there was passing me the ball.

128
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:29,420
Have these guys always been this strong?
Really? But I thought scoring 3 points was better than just 2...

129
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:33,540
This team... I think they might actually be able
to go to the inter-high...

130
00:08:37,710 --> 00:08:40,710
Crap! The inter-high doesn't 
matter at all right now!

131
00:08:40,710 --> 00:08:43,000
I forgot that my body is on the line!

132
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,880
Rebound!

133
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,040
Yo, Kite! Don't just let them 
shoot an open three like that!

134
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:01,420
Shut it.

135
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,750
Did you even hear what I said?! Hey!

136
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:09,500
I don't think we can win this...

137
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,500
I feel really bad for Madoka...

138
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,330
Come on, don't give up!

139
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:15,130
Hey, Madoka!

140
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:18,790
From here on out, just stick to my plan.

141
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:21,920
Nao...

142
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:25,080
Okay! Go, girls!

143
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:31,880
What now?

144
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,460
Zone defense?!

145
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,750
What does that mean?

146
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:48,670
Just look.

147
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:52,500
As you can see here, "Zone defense"
is when the entire team

148
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:56,210
focuses solely on defending 
the area around the basket.

149
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,330
Unlike man-to-man, which requires everyone
to constantly guard a specific player,

150
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:04,880
this style makes them all responsible for guarding
a specific "zone" instead, hence the name.

151
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,290
That makes sense.

152
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:07,000
But then...

153
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:09,880
what good does that actually do?

154
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:12,040
No way, they can't be serious.

155
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,880
Did they forget we have Sora on our team?

156
00:10:14,170 --> 00:10:15,330
What does he mean?

157
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:20,290
The major difference between zone and man-to-man,
is that the area the defense guards is limited.

158
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:23,420
In exchange for preventing anyone
on the other team from reaching the paint,

159
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:25,670
it becomes easier for them to score
from long distance instead.

160
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:29,540
Simply put, the single most effective way
to neutralize a zone defense

161
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:33,210
is by having a really skilled
3-point shooter, just like Sora.

162
00:10:33,210 --> 00:10:36,880
I get it. That means our resident shorty
will be doing most of the work from now on.

163
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:40,080
Unfortunately for you, it's 
not going to be that simple.

164
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:42,790
Because...

165
00:10:43,830 --> 00:10:46,250
...this is not an ordinary zone defense.

166
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:48,880
Box and 1.

167
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:54,210
Using this will enable us to prevent both Natsume
and Kurumatani from scoring any more points.

168
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:06,630
Box and 1, eh?

169
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:09,790
Well, that's the most obvious decision
they could have made.

170
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,880
Yabuuchi is moving alone and 
totally ignoring her area.

171
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:15,710
Doesn't that ruin this 
whole "zone defense" thing?

172
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,080
Nope.

173
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:20,130
It's a variation, which means
it's still considered a zone defense.

174
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,880
While four of the players focus on defending their zones,
the last one goes man-to-man

175
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,960
with the one opponent who poses
the biggest scoring threat.

176
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:30,330
This allows them to effectively suppress
the ace of the other team.

177
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:34,420
Even if that player gets a hold of the ball,
all 5 can work to defend against them.

178
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:36,170
That's the box and 1 defense.

179
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:41,540
So, 3-pointers are out of the question.

180
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:43,830
Our best bet is to follow standard practice
and exploit it with passes.

181
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:47,290
But if their defense is this 
clustered together, then...

182
00:11:50,630 --> 00:11:52,330
Did you get all that, Madoka?

183
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:56,920
This defense is designed so that
it's impossible to shoot any threes.

184
00:11:57,290 --> 00:12:00,290
Our first step is to shut down
their top scorer, Kurumatani.

185
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,420
Yo! Don't push through! Just pass it around!

186
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:05,790
I can do it!

187
00:12:08,670 --> 00:12:11,040
We can already assume that 
he'll find a way past you.

188
00:12:11,290 --> 00:12:15,290
But letting him go past the three-point line
will actually make everything work in our favor.

189
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:19,750
They may be able to stop me from shooting threes,
but I can still charge-in and shoot from mid-range!

190
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:22,880
They reacted fast!

191
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,670
What the hell was that?! You damn shrimp!

192
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:35,670
Well shit, they snatched it right from us.

193
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:38,960
One fundamental aspect of zone defense
is reacting to the ball instead of to other players.

194
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:44,670
Unless the opposing team is good at passing
the ball around, then steals are more likely to occur.

195
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:48,080
Are you serious? Then that means
there's hardly anything they can do.

196
00:12:48,290 --> 00:12:50,830
And we haven't even gotten 
to the good part yet.

197
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:58,960
Huh?

198
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:02,000
Is it just me, or is everybody 
getting clustered on the left?

199
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,250
Kite is one thing, but even 
Chiaki is over there now.

200
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,380
I know what's up!

201
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:08,630
They're pushing the offense 
to one side of the court!

202
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,250
Sora got a taste of that back in our match
with Maru High, remember?

203
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:24,170
I'm gonna get the ball back!

204
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:26,630
That's it, stray frustrated.

205
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:28,830
And then chase after me like a good boy!

206
00:13:31,170 --> 00:13:32,040
Oh crap!

207
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,330
A screen!

208
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,420
Dammit!

209
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,210
Idiot! Don't follow her!

210
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:44,630
That was way too close.

211
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:47,210
She nearly slipped away 
from me in an instant.

212
00:13:53,130 --> 00:13:54,040
Gotta stop it!

213
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:04,130
Dammit! Going one-on-one right below the basket
is too hard at my height!

214
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,580
Nice shot, Madoka!

215
00:14:08,210 --> 00:14:09,080
Huh?

216
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:12,330
How did all you guys end up so far away?

217
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,960
You dummy.

218
00:14:14,710 --> 00:14:16,670
Don't just walk into such an obvious trap.

219
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:20,330
They wanted you to be the one who went
under the basket and you fell for it.

220
00:14:20,630 --> 00:14:21,540
No way...

221
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:26,250
That tiny lady over there, planned a strategy
that assures they can score points.

222
00:14:27,170 --> 00:14:28,630
It was an isolation play.

223
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,630
"Isolation play"?

224
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:36,080
Facing our man-to-man defense, they spread out across
the court and create empty space below the basket.

225
00:14:39,330 --> 00:14:42,460
Then someone sets up a screen
and quickly returns to their position,

226
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,210
forcing the pair in that 
space to go one-on-one.

227
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:48,540
That's known as an isolation play.

228
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:52,790
They all know that you're not
an effective guard underneath the basket.

229
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:55,330
Do you get it now?

230
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:58,960
The other team is taking full advantage
of your lack of height.

231
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:03,500
Tee-hee~

232
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:07,130
What the heck is that?! 
What does it even mean?!

233
00:15:07,710 --> 00:15:09,080
It was really cute, though.

234
00:15:09,330 --> 00:15:11,630
If they set up another screen on the shrimp,

235
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:15,710
we have to execute a solid switch or else they're
just going to keep abusing his shortness to score.

236
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:17,290
Yeah, I know.

237
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,210
What the hell's a "switch"?

238
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,920
Dude, that's easy. The thing on the wall
that turns out the lights.

239
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,250
It means switching up defenders on the fly!

240
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,380
"Switching up defenders on the fly"?

241
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:29,540
Whenever you're playing man-to-man defense,

242
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:34,580
everyone has to be ready to change the player they're
defending to deal with screens from the other team.

243
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,920
That's called a "switch."

244
00:15:36,210 --> 00:15:41,420
Out on the court you have to say "switch!" or something
else, to let everyone know that you're changing.

245
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:43,130
O-oh...

246
00:15:43,130 --> 00:15:48,540
If they pull another screen like that on you, then I'll
switch to defending Yabuuchi since I'm taller than her.

247
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:49,630
Got it?

248
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:50,710
Right!

249
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,920
Keep your eyes on them!

250
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:55,960
Right!

251
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,000
Close their pass windows!

252
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,380
Dammit!

253
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:03,170
I don't even have the ball yet!

254
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:06,170
This is just like what happened
in our match against Maru High!

255
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,830
Hey, Bro, give it here!

256
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,580
Getting past four of them should be a cinch!

257
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:15,460
Listen carefully.

258
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:20,170
Whenever Natsume makes a move to penetrate to the
basket, we'll use all four defenders to shut him down.

259
00:16:20,790 --> 00:16:25,290
First, one defender will immediately stick to him
to prevent any shots from middle-range.

260
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:28,670
If he gets around them, then the remaining three
will triple team to put on pressure.

261
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,250
The first defender will also press him from behind
to assure he'll have no windows to pass through.

262
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:38,250
But if we do that, won't he just pass it
the instant that we try to triple team him?

263
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:39,880
Don't worry about that.

264
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:41,880
I know he won't pass it.

265
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:49,000
Kite! They left me wide open over here!

266
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,420
I'm the one... who's going to score!

267
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:01,460
Boys
Girls

268
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:01,040
Offensive foul! Charging!

269
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:03,580
Ow, ow, ow...

270
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:05,380
Oh my gosh! Are you all right, Sachi?

271
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:08,080
Give me a break, it can't be that bad.

272
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:10,170
That was a totally reckless 
move and you know it!

273
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,130
Nabe was wide open right behind you!

274
00:17:12,710 --> 00:17:14,380
Why the hell are you playing lone wolf?

275
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:18,290
Well, I probably would have missed the basket
even if he did pass it...

276
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:22,750
Even if he can't shoot well, passing the ball to him
would definitely have spread out the defense.

277
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,130
And that Kite guy is way too skilled to not know
something that fundamental about the game.

278
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:28,040
I wonder why he didn't just pass the ball?

279
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:31,500
Man, I bet you that he still doesn't trust
the other members of the team.

280
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:35,000
Nah, I would say it's because he's
overconfident in his ability to score.

281
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:37,710
Actually, it's a mix of both.

282
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:42,460
He feels a strong sense of responsibility as a forward,
and that comes from confidence in his skills.

283
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:48,290
When someone has the level of talent that he does,
it's only natural that it can become a weakness at times.

284
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,250
Another screen?!

285
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:55,290
Don't bother, Sora! We're switching!

286
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,710
Timeout for the boys' team!

287
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:17,670
Nice! You pulled that 
pass off perfectly, Yoko!

288
00:18:17,670 --> 00:18:19,330
Senpai!

289
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:23,000
Ugh! I can't believe you guys
actually made me shoot a 3-pointer!

290
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,830
My hands are still shaking with anxiety!

291
00:18:26,130 --> 00:18:30,330
This time they gave up heading
for the paint and just shot a three instead.

292
00:18:31,710 --> 00:18:34,750
They're determined to take advantage
of Sora's height for this whole game.

293
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,750
Hmph, that damned tiny lady.
She's better than I gave her credit for.

294
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:39,710
Dammit...

295
00:18:39,710 --> 00:18:43,460
It's all because of me that we're being hindered
on both offense and defense.

296
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:46,540
What the hell happened
to all that momentum we had earlier?

297
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:49,420
All our dreams of that bra falling to the floor
are slowly fading away...

298
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:52,420
Shucks, I really can't 
keep up with any of this.

299
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:55,330
I had a sneaking suspicion
that this might be the case, but...

300
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,170
...we're all still really weak
when it comes to basketball, huh?

301
00:18:59,170 --> 00:19:03,500
Seriously, I doubt we're even at the level
of being able to compete in a real game yet.

302
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:06,330
I mean, there's only four guys on our team
with actual experience.

303
00:19:06,330 --> 00:19:07,500
What?

304
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:10,710
I don't remember saying anything
about you guys being weak.

305
00:19:10,710 --> 00:19:11,540
Huh?

306
00:19:11,710 --> 00:19:14,330
Your team is... really strong.

307
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,420
I'm sorry, Kurumatani.

308
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,960
But...

309
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:25,630
Oh jeez. Now's not the time
to be having a pity party, guys.

310
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:31,290
There'll be no stripping at this rate, much less,
any chance of us going to the inter-high!

311
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:34,250
Just let me handle our next move.

312
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:38,420
It looks like Afro Senpai is 
cooking up some kind of plan.

313
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:43,040
How exactly will they try
and counter the box and 1 defense?

314
00:19:43,670 --> 00:19:45,040
Let you handle it?

315
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:48,670
But we haven't done any practice
to overcome a zone defense...

316
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:51,670
That's a good point. So for now...

317
00:19:52,210 --> 00:19:53,670
You two, sub out!

318
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:55,580
S-sub out?!

319
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,380
But why us?!

320
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:00,500
Bro! At least tell us what your reason is!

321
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,420
Because you're in the way.

322
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,460
Huh?!

323
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:05,500
Hell yeah! It's time for the real 
superstars to hit the court!

324
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,130
I've been waiting for this!

325
00:20:07,130 --> 00:20:09,540
Wait! I haven't agreed to 
sub out with anyone ye-

326
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:12,960
Player substitution!

327
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:17,540
Here we go, my blood has 
already started pumping.

328
00:20:18,170 --> 00:20:19,380
Dammit...

329
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:22,290
Why would they take
their two primary scorers out of the game?

330
00:20:22,790 --> 00:20:24,830
It's almost like they're 
trying to throw the match.

331
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:28,750
This is nothing new, we never know
what those idiots are thinking.

332
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,790
Listen up, Momoharu.

333
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:36,040
The only members of the team now
who can put up a screen are you and me.

334
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:38,290
Let's do what we can to 
tear their defense apart.

335
00:20:38,290 --> 00:20:39,790
Uh, right.

336
00:20:40,130 --> 00:20:42,500
We're gonna.... win this thing!

337
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,290
No question!

338
00:20:48,130 --> 00:20:50,630
I've had enough! No more pervy stares!

339
00:20:50,630 --> 00:20:51,880
You damn horndogs!

340
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:56,130
All right! Time to get back on track, boys!

341
00:20:57,330 --> 00:20:58,960
Let's go, let's go!

342
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,540
Dammit! Why can't I play?!

343
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:04,750
This is clearly a terrible strategy!

344
00:21:05,710 --> 00:21:06,920
Not at all.

345
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,500
I think he made the perfect 
call for this situation.

346
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:15,210
If you both stayed out there, it would have been
impossible to overcome the box and 1 defense.

347
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:25,130
The 2-3 zone.

348
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:28,250
It's the most commonly used formation
when playing zone defense.

349
00:21:28,630 --> 00:21:32,790
And it'll be difficult for these guys to deal with,
since none of them are long-range shooters.

350
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:36,380
With Yasu on the court, we have
a pretty big height advantage on them.

351
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:38,170
Let's just pass the ball over their heads an-

352
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:39,880
No, we won't bother with that.

353
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,920
We can't afford to turn this into
a height competition between boys and girls.

354
00:21:44,170 --> 00:21:46,380
We have to play this on equal 
ground until the very end.

355
00:21:47,710 --> 00:21:50,040
Otherwise, there's no point
to playing with our current lineup.

356
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:52,040
I have no doubt about it.

357
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,080
That guy has also...

358
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:57,290
...realized all the weaknesses 
of the players on this team!

359
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:18,580
It didn't matter how long 
you stared up at the sky

360
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:21,880
You always said that you 
would never be able to fly

361
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:25,080
One night I cried wondering 
how long it would take

362
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:28,460
Until I could finally reach you with my hands

363
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,960
Eventually I got used to just running away

364
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:35,250
Until the day I realized that was a weakness

365
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:39,460
So let's start it all over, right now

366
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:48,080
The things precious to us 
were always close at hand

367
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:54,420
We are never completely alone 
at any time in our lives

368
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:57,750
The truth is that you can 
fly, wherever you want

369
00:22:57,750 --> 00:23:01,500
Spreading your wings to go 
far higher than anyone else

370
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:05,750
The more tears that you shed

371
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,710
Then the stronger you become

372
00:23:07,710 --> 00:23:11,080
Let's use those wings 
to travel the world over

373
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:14,670
And find a path to a future 
that no one knows about

374
00:23:14,670 --> 00:23:19,250
Always, always, always

375
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:22,920
Walking onwards, all of us together

376
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Team

377
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:33,710
Next time: "Team."

